# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is a boot wrapper (/boot.sh) that starts unbound in the
# BACKGROUND (self-daemonized, no `-d`), polls until :53 answers, then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the resolver is ALREADY RUNNING as an open resolver with version disclosure
#     when the agent starts, which is what makes the "edited unbound.conf but
#     never restarted unbound" case detectable (unbound reads config only at
#     startup);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity` (tini reaps unbound), so restarting unbound
#     cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART unbound (kill + relaunch), not
# merely start it if absent - it is already up with the vulnerable configuration.
# Do NOT kill PID 1.
